	<text xml:lang="la">
		<note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" subtype="metadata" n="1">"Epistola nuncupatoria" zu Geßners ungedrucktem Werk "Thrinodiae sive sacra magnanimi herois <persName ref="p4091" cert="high">Huldrychi Zvinglii</persName>, patris patriae fortissimi" vom August 1532 (Zürich ZB, Ms C 50a, 334r.-341v., Nr. 65).</note>
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>Doctissimis, clarissimis et integerrimis viris <persName ref="p495">Henrico <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>Bullingero</persName> et <persName ref="p8171">Theodoro Bibliandro</persName>, <placeName ref="l587">Tiguri</placeName> <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>munus <persName ref="p4091">Huldrychi Zvinglii</persName>, herois invictissimi, <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>sustinentibus<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2"><persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> war <persName ref="p4091">Zwinglis</persName> Nachfolger im kirchlichen, <persName ref="p8171">Bibliander</persName> im schulischen Amt; vgl. <bibl source="b292">HBRG</bibl> I 306.</note>, praeceptoribus et patronis colendis, <lb xml:id="p1z5"/><persName ref="p1283">Conradus Gessnerus</persName> salutem etc.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z6"/>Quotiescunque animo meo, praeceptores reverendi, <lb xml:id="p1z7"/>summam illam nostrae aetatis ingratitudinem vo<lb xml:id="p1z8"/>lutare coepero, dictu mirum, quanto mens mea <lb xml:id="p1z9"/>dolore tota inuratur.</s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">„Tam rara in amicitiis fides, <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>tam parata oblivio mortuorum“, ut <persName ref="p18983">Plinii</persName> verbis<note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3"><persName ref="p18983">Plinius</persName>, Epistulae, 6, 10, 5.</note> ut<lb xml:id="p1z11"/>ar.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la">Neque enim ullus est nostrorum, qui vel unico <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>verbulo gratum aperiat animum erga strenuissim<lb xml:id="p1z13"/>um illum heroem, patrem patriae lucemque <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>orbis terrarum <persName ref="p4091">Huldrychum Zvinglium</persName><note xml:id="fnb" type="footnote" n="b"><persName ref="p4091">Huldrychum Zvinglium</persName> <hi>in Majuskeln.</hi></note>, <lb xml:id="p1z15"/>in cuius vestigiis (quod toti <placeName ref="l587">Tigurinum</placeName> reipublicae <lb xml:id="p1z16"/>foeliciter cedat) vos quoque nunc insistitis.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">Hero<lb xml:id="p1z17"/>em merito appello, utpote quem nulla unquam vis, <lb xml:id="p1z18"/>nullae minae, nullae insidiae, nulla denique invidia <lb xml:id="p1z19"/>a vero et honesto labefecerit.</s>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la">Itaque non solum <lb xml:id="p1z20"/>verbis laudari, verum etiam auro, ebore, argento <lb xml:id="p1z21"/><placeName ref="l1040">Parioque</placeName> marmore<note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4">Der Marmor von der griechischen Insel <placeName ref="l1040">Paros</placeName> galt als besonders hochwertig; vgl. <bibl source="b4">HBBW II</bibl> <ref target="file10150">[Nr. 119]</ref>, S. 173f, Anm. 5.</note> effingi dignissimus erat.</s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">Ille, <lb xml:id="p1z22"/>inquam, heros, vir solidae laudis, perfectae cumu<lb xml:id="p1z23"/>lataeque virtutis, cum apud exteras gentes summo <lb xml:id="p1z24"/>honore celebretur, apud nos tamen solos, de quibus <lb xml:id="p1z25"/>maxime omnium bene meritus est, iacet; nullus <lb xml:id="p1z26"/>ei honos, reverentia nulla, nulla prorsus bene<lb xml:id="p1z27"/>f<pb type="scan" next="335v."/> icioru<pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>m <lb xml:id="p2z2"/>ei gratia habetur.</s>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la">Illud est, quod doleo, quod <lb xml:id="p2z3"/>me maxime movet <foreign xml:lang="el">ϕίλον τετιηµένον ἦτορ</foreign><note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5">Vgl. <persName ref="p18514">Homer</persName>, Odyssee, 1, 114 u. ö.</note>.</s>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la">Eius enim <lb xml:id="p2z4"/>dum saltem audio nomen, vox mea fletu debi<lb xml:id="p2z5"/>litatur, mensque tota dolore impeditur.</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la">Ferrei <lb xml:id="p2z6"/>ille profecto, immo impii fuerit animi, quem <lb xml:id="p2z7"/>tanta totius christianae reipublicae clades non mo<lb xml:id="p2z8"/>verit.</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la">Virum enim amisimus, cui similis nostro <lb xml:id="p2z9"/>seculo nemo fuit, dicere priori religio est<note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" n="6">Man scheut sich zu sagen, in der vorigen Epoche.</note>.</s>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la">Ille enim <lb xml:id="p2z10"/>in omni virtute facile princeps, eruditus utili<lb xml:id="p2z11"/>a miscere honestis<note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7">Vgl. <persName ref="p18648">Tacitus</persName>, Agricola, 8, 1.</note>, iura, iudicia, leges edoctus <lb xml:id="p2z12"/>et arma, Christi ecclesiae non minori iustitia <lb xml:id="p2z13"/>quam fortitudine pręfuit vir intelligentia magna, <lb xml:id="p2z14"/>veritate maiori, fide maxima praeditus.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p2z15"/>Cui exiguum vitae curriculum natura circum<lb xml:id="p2z16"/>scripsit, immensum gloriae; quam sane quanto mi<lb xml:id="p2z17"/>nus ambiit, tanto magis illam vivam et per<lb xml:id="p2z18"/>petuam habiturus est apud omnes fideles, <lb xml:id="p2z19"/><foreign xml:lang="el">οἷς ἀγαθὴ κραδίη καὶ πείθεται ἀθανάτοισι</foreign>, <lb xml:id="p2z20"/>ut poeta ait<note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8">Orphica, Lithica, 5.</note>.</s>
					<s n="14" xml:lang="la">Acerbius equidem mortem strenu<lb xml:id="p2z21"/>issimi herois tulissem, nisi ipsum scirem <lb xml:id="p2z22"/>certo exultare et gaudere cum Christo cunctis<lb xml:id="p2z23"/>que beatis, <foreign xml:lang="el">οἳ ὀυρανὸν ἐυρὺν ἔχουσιν</foreign><note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" n="9"><persName ref="p18514">Homer</persName>, Odyssee, 4, 378; 22, 39.</note>.</s>
					<s n="15" xml:lang="el"><lb xml:id="p2z24"/>Αἲ γὰρ ἐγὼν ὣς ε<lb xml:id="p2z25"/>ἴην ἀθανάτος καὶ ἀγήραος ἤµα<lb xml:id="p2z26"/>τα πάντα<note xml:id="fn10" type="footnote" n="10"><persName ref="p18514">Homer</persName>, Ilias, 8, 538f.</note> ὣς ἐνὶ ἀθανάτοισι θεοίσι Ζουίγγ<lb xml:id="p2z27"/>λιε <pb/><lb xml:id="p3z1"/>χαίρεις.<pb type="edition" next="43"/></s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="16" xml:lang="la"><pb type="scan" next="336r."/><lb xml:id="p3z2"/>Vivit semperque vigebit, nulla aetas, nulla un<lb xml:id="p3z3"/>quam dies memoriam poterit extinguere <persName ref="p4091">Zvinglii</persName>, „<lb xml:id="p3z4"/>cuius placido posuere in pectore sedem <lb xml:id="p3z5"/>blandus honos hilarisque tamen cum pondere virtus.“<note xml:id="fn11" type="footnote" n="11"><persName ref="p20993">Statius</persName>, Silvae, 2, 3, 64f.</note></s>
					<s n="17" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p3z6"/>Nec coelos nec terras tanti herois oblivio capi<lb xml:id="p3z7"/>et unquam, siquidem in terris nunquam deficiet <lb xml:id="p3z8"/>eius gloria et fama, <foreign xml:lang="el">ἣ ἐκ διός ἐστι βροτοῖσι</foreign><note xml:id="fn12" type="footnote" n="12">Vgl. <persName ref="p18514">Homer</persName>, Ilias, 2, 197.</note>.</s>
					<s n="18" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p3z9"/>In coelis vero perpetuo cum Helia, Davide et Abra<lb xml:id="p3z10"/>hamo, immo cum Christo ipso vivit immortalis <lb xml:id="p3z11"/><persName ref="p4091">Zvinglii</persName> gaudetque anima.</s>
					<s n="19" xml:lang="el"><foreign xml:lang="la">Verum hęc hactenus</foreign>; <lb xml:id="p3z12"/>ἁπλοῦς γάρ ἐστι τῆς ἀληθείας λόγος<note xml:id="fn13" type="footnote" n="13">Vgl. <persName ref="p20284">Aischylos</persName>, Fragmenta, 176 (Tragicorum Graecorum Fragmenta, Bd. 3: Aischylos, hg. v. Stefan Radt, Göttingen 1985, S. 290); Adagia, 1, 3, 88 (LB II 145f).</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="20" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p3z13"/>Mitto itaque vobis, viri ornatissimi, illas <persName ref="p4091">Huldrychi <lb xml:id="p3z14"/>Zvinglii</persName> <foreign xml:lang="el">θρηνῳδίας</foreign>, tenuis nostri agel<lb xml:id="p3z15"/>li primitias, quas vobis maxime dedicare li<lb xml:id="p3z16"/>buit, qui nobis indignis erepti<note xml:id="fnc" type="footnote" n="c"><hi>vor</hi> erepti <hi>gestrichenes</hi> summ.</note> herois <lb xml:id="p3z17"/>summa cum diligentia et fide munus obitis.</s>
					<s n="21" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p3z18"/>Ideo autem mitto, ut saltem aliquod grati animi <lb xml:id="p3z19"/>specimen erga virum<note xml:id="fnd" type="footnote" n="d"><hi>vor</hi> virum <hi>gestrichenes</hi> nostrę patretię[?] in.</note> tam praeclare <lb xml:id="p3z20"/>de nostra <placeName ref="l862">Helvetia</placeName> meritum vobis offerrem, non <lb xml:id="p3z21"/>tanquam ulla laus tanto viro per me accedere possit.</s>
					<s n="22" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p3z22"/>Qui sane vir nunquam <foreign xml:lang="el">ἐµεῦ ζῶντος καὶ ἐπὶ χθονὶ <lb xml:id="p3z23"/>δερκοµένοιο</foreign><note xml:id="fn14" type="footnote" n="14">Homer, Ilias, 1, 88.</note> puerili mea memoria elabetur.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="23" xml:lang="la">Rogatam <lb xml:id="p3z24"/>itaque cupio c[elsitudinem] v[estram], ut, quiccquid id sit, animo benig<lb xml:id="p3z25"/>no accipiat et barbariei nostrae veniam det.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="24" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell">Va<lb xml:id="p3z26"/>lete meque alumnum vestrum semper, ut coepistis, <lb xml:id="p3z27"/>fovete.</s>
					<s n="25" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l491">Argentinae</placeName>, in aedibus d[octoris] <persName ref="p5565">Wolphgangi Fa<lb xml:id="p3z28"/>britii Capitonis</persName>, 10. augusti anno 1532.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="26" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p3z29"/>V[estrae] c[elsitudini] deditissimus <lb xml:id="p3z30"/><persName ref="p1283">Conradus Gessnerus</persName>.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
		</body>
